2 allows me to focus on a Half Flush or potentially Full Flush pattern using bamboo tiles (T suit) which are well-connected (T1-T7 with duplicates). The J2 pair doesn't contribute significantly to high-scoring patterns, and keeping it limits my flexibility. With T9 completely exhausted, I cannot achieve Pure Straight. By discarding J2, I can work toward patterns like Half Flush (6 points) + All Chows (2 points) = 8 points minimum, which is exactly the threshold needed to win.\n\nAnswer: Play J2"}
